{"availability":"available","full":"alexfalkowski/go-service","name":"go-service","description":"A framework to build services in Go.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":34,"forks":3,"created":"2021-05-02T14:28:46Z","updated":"2026-10-09T08:46:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://alexfalkowski.github.io/go-service","topics":["cache","cloudevents","golang","grpc","http","mvc","postgres","redis","rpc"],"demo":"https://alexfalkowski.github.io/go-service","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:48.529Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:48.529Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:48.529Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:04:48.529Z","stars":34,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["github.com/alexfalkowski/go-service/v2 is an opinionated framework/library for building Go services with consistent wiring for configuration, DI, transports, telemetry, crypto, etc.","This repo is primarily a library of packages (no top-level cmd/ binary). Services built on top typically define their own main package elsewhere and import this module.","Long-running services are expected to start from go-service-template, while short-lived client commands start from go-client-template. Both compose the high-level module bundles from this repository. These are the primary supported paths. Lower-level package-by-package composition is still available, but it is an advanced mode and may require extra manual registration."],"features":["feature.Config embeds client-side config (config/client.Config): address, timeout, retry, breaker, limiter, TLS, token, and options. This repository does not construct a built-in OpenFeature provider from this config —…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alexfalkowski/go-service/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"5fbde22870b4a22252fee2ae66024569649014d366e7fc6bd415c8004c9947b0","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:48.661Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10